{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":203,"description":"Dead-code params: `livePreview` and `livePreviewContentTypeUid` are added to IContentstackGetEntry and consumed via addParam inside getEntry, but no caller anywhere in the codebase passes these values. The prescribed fix states: 'pass the live preview query parameters from the incoming request (typically live_preview and content_type_uid from URL search params) to the ContentstackFactory query.' The diff adds the receiving end but never wires the sending end — no getStaticProps/getServerSideProps/middleware extracts live_preview or content_type_uid from the request URL and passes them to getEntry. The addParam block is unreachable in production. AC1 ('rendered page displays the entry's content') is not met because draft content is never fetched.","suggestedFix":"Wire the request-to-getEntry path. In the page-level data fetching function (getStaticProps/getServerSideProps or equivalent), extract live_preview and content_type_uid from the URL search params (e.g., context.query.live_preview, context.query.content_type_uid) and pass them through to every getEntry call that should support preview. Alternatively, if the Contentstack SDK's live_preview config automatically injects preview params when enable:true, verify this with the SDK docs and remove the manual addParam code — but do not leave dead-code params on the interface."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":203,"description":"Duplicated addParam logic — concision violation. The exact same 6-line addParam block is copy-pasted in two places within getEntry (the initial query at line ~203 and the pagination-loop query at line ~226). A more concise change: add livePreview and livePreviewContentTypeUid to ICommonContentstackConfig and apply addParam inside setCommonConfig (which is already called by createContentTypeQuery). This eliminates the duplication, ensures the params are forwarded on every query path, and is fewer lines of code.","suggestedFix":"Add `livePreview?: string` and `livePreviewContentTypeUid?: string` to ICommonContentstackConfig. In setCommonConfig, after the existing config application, add: `if (config.livePreview) { query.addParam('live_preview', config.livePreview); if (config.livePreviewContentTypeUid) query.addParam('content_type_uid', config.livePreviewContentTypeUid); }`. Then remove the duplicated blocks from getEntry and pass the params through the existing createContentTypeQuery call's commonConfig spread."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":63,"description":"No vitest unit tests added for the new live_preview configuration or the addParam forwarding logic. The diff adds 7 lines of SDK config and ~12 lines of addParam forwarding, but zero test files. Per review criteria, new features must have corresponding vitest unit tests in test/unit/ mirroring the src/ path. There are no tests verifying: (a) options.live_preview.enable is true when CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW==='true', (b) options.live_preview.host equals CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST, (c) options.live_preview.management_token equals CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN, (d) getEntry calls addParam with live_preview and content_type_uid when livePreview is provided, (e) getEntry does not call addParam when livePreview is absent.","suggestedFix":"Create test/unit/services/contentstack.spec.ts (or add to existing test file) with test cases covering: (1) options object includes live_preview with correct enable/host/management_token from env vars, (2) enable is false when CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW is not 'true', (3) getEntry forwards livePreview and livePreviewContentTypeUid via addParam, (4) getEntry does not call addParam when livePreview is undefined."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":260,"description":"getSingleEntry, getSingletonEntry, and findSingletonEntry do not accept or forward livePreview/livePreviewContentTypeUid params. If any page renders content via these functions (e.g., single entry pages, singleton content types), live preview will not work for those pages — the SDK will return only published content. This partially fails AC1 for any content type fetched through these paths.","suggestedFix":"Add livePreview and livePreviewContentTypeUid to IContentstackGetSingleEntry and IContentstackGetSingletonEntry (they already extend IContentstackGetEntry, so the interface is covered). Then forward the params via addParam in getSingleEntry and findSingletonEntry, or better, use the setCommonConfig approach from the concision fix above so all query paths automatically forward preview params."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/interface/contentstack.ts","line":27,"description":"livePreview is typed as `string | boolean` but addParam('live_preview', livePreview) passes the value directly to the Contentstack SDK, which expects a string. If a caller passes `true` (boolean), the SDK may serialize it incorrectly or reject it. The URL search param is always a string, so the type should be `string` only.","suggestedFix":"Change `livePreview?: string | boolean` to `livePreview?: string` in IContentstackGetEntry."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":204,"description":"Unnecessary type assertion: `(_query as contentstack.Query).addParam(...)`. The query returned by factory.createContentTypeQuery() is already a contentstack.Query (or a subtype). The cast suggests a type mismatch that should be resolved at the return-type level of createContentTypeQuery rather than patched with an assertion. If setCommonConfig is used (per the concision fix), the query parameter there is typed as `contentstack.Query | contentstack.Entry` — addParam is only on Query, so a type guard or method check would be safer than a blanket cast.","suggestedFix":"Ensure createContentTypeQuery returns a type that includes addParam (e.g., the return type of .toJSON() in the Contentstack SDK). If the SDK's type definitions don't expose addParam on the toJSON result, use a minimal interface extension rather than `as contentstack.Query`."}],"summary":"The diff correctly adds the live_preview SDK configuration to the Stack options (matching the first part of the prescribed fix) and adds addParam forwarding in getEntry (matching the second part). However, three blockers prevent merge: (1) No caller wires request URL params to getEntry's new livePreview/livePreviewContentTypeUid parameters — the addParam code is dead code and draft content is never fetched, failing AC1. (2) The addParam logic is duplicated in two places within getEntry — a more concise approach (forwarding via setCommonConfig) would eliminate the duplication and cover all query paths. (3) No unit tests exist for the new functionality. Additionally, getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry/findSingletonEntry are not updated to forward preview params, which is a major gap for pages using those functions."}
